[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":108},["ShallowReactive",2],{"/nw/bicomponent-clusters":3,"/nw/bicomponent-clusters-surround":97},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"description":63,"extension":64,"meta":65,"navigation":83,"path":93,"seo":94,"stem":95,"__hash__":96},"content/nw/bicomponent-clusters.md","Networks Extension Dictionary: bicomponent-clusters",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":53},"minimark",[9],[10,11,15,16,15,26,42],"div",{"className":12,"id":14},[13],"dict_entry","bicomponent-clusters","\n  ",[17,18,20,21,15],"h3",{"id":19},"nwbicomponent-clusters","\n    ",[22,23,25],"a",{"href":24},"#bicomponent-clusters","nw:bicomponent-clusters",[27,28,32],"h4",{"id":29,"className":30},"nwbicomponent-clusters-1",[31],"section-heading",[22,33,20,37,15],{"className":34,"href":36},[35],"section-anchor","#----nwbicomponent-clusters---1",[38,39,25],"span",{"className":40},[41],"prim_example",[43,44,45,46,52],"p",{},"Reports the list of ",[22,47,51],{"href":48,"rel":49},"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biconnected_component",[50],"nofollow","bicomponent clusters"," in the current network context. A bicomponent (also known as a maximal biconnected subgraph) is a part of a network that cannot be disconnected by removing only one node (i.e. you need to remove at least two to disconnect it). The result is reported as a list of agentsets, in random order. Note that one turtle can be a member of more than one bicomponent at once.",{"title":54,"searchDepth":55,"depth":56,"links":57},"",5,3,[58],{"id":19,"depth":56,"text":59,"children":60},"\n    nw:bicomponent-clusters\n  ",[61],{"id":29,"depth":62,"text":59},4,"Documentation for the bicomponent-clusters primitive.","md",{"source":66,"metadataOutputPath":67,"projectConfig":68,"language":76,"inheritFrom":84,"output":83,"version":69,"layout":85,"dictionaryDisplayName":86,"dictionaryHomeDirectory":87,"indexFileURI":88,"currentItemId":14,"currentItemLabel":25,"primRoot":89,"icon":90,"extensionName":91,"assetsRoot":71},"../../external/extensions/nw/nw/bic